  "boundaries": [
    "This change commits hepta-evidence qualification-facade effect history for Agentd kernel.evidence recovery admission. It does not compose AutomationStore runtime state, budget reservation, FinalUse consumption and external execution into one transaction.",
    "A current checkpoint must come from an independent fresh state source. A same-host fixture or path outside Agent home does not establish a fresh failure domain; rollback of all replicas and checkpoints remains outside the guarantee.",
    "No online witness service, expected-old checkpoint CAS, transparency-log consistency proof, or availability qualification is supplied by this patch.",
    "V1 recovery checkpoints are refused; an authorized publisher must review and re-sign V2. Trust-file schema remains V1 and recovery identity remains Ed25519.",
    "The frontier reads 256-row pages and caps total effect rows at 1,000,000. This is neither a strict byte-memory limit nor a bound for all startup verification; existing cold-open verification still fetches all effect rows.",
    "Snapshot validation rechecks actual JSON bytes against their stored digests. It does not enforce canonical JSON reserialization or replace existing typed/column-projection checks.",
    "External effects without idempotency or result lookup still require an unresolved state; no arbitrary exactly-once guarantee is established."
  ],
